From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] oleacc: IAccIdentity on window objects, annotation table reader (3583)

oleacc: IAccIdentity on the window objects, read side of the annotation table

The client, window and non-client part objects answer IAccIdentity: GetIdentityString gives the identity string
of (window, object id, child id) in the form ComposeHwndIdentityString makes. A Wine-private export,
WineAccPropGetValue, reads the IAccPropServices table (a stored value, or the answer of a registered
IAccPropServer). Property servers are kept in the global interface table, so a reader on any thread gets an
interface usable in its own apartment (a server registered from an MTA thread of an apartment-threaded
CAccPropServices was otherwise a proxy of the wrong apartment).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XZFS4SPPzeH5d2c1MuzqCS
---
